> When io.ReadFull() below doesn't read the bytes fully (returning ErrUnexpectedEOF), the next invocation of Decode() must not decode the record header.

But when `ErrUnexpectedEOF` is returned from `readFull`, the `maxDecodeRetry` loop continues to read the bytes from the reader till the length is read fully, no?

