```

It exactly illustrates the problem, when reading the msgLen:
 * `EOF` when reading the length of the message is fatal when we already read more than one byte from the stream. The reason is that this would advance the stream and the next call to `Decode()` would read a new length from a starting position incremented by one
and when reading the message itself:
 * `EOF` here is not valid even if read=0 because the length has already been read so if we exit here the next `Decode` will try to start reading a new msg length from somewhere inside the message.
